  "id": "ecological-systems-theory",
  "term": "ecological systems theory",
  "definition": "Ecological systems theory is a developmental view that understands behavior and outcomes as shaped by multiple parts of a person’s social environment, from close relationships like family and peers to broader settings such as neighborhoods and public policy. It highlights that both nearby and more distant influences work together to affect development.",
